-module(libsodium_crypto_core_ristretto255).
-moduledoc """
Low-level arithmetic on the ristretto255 prime-order group (RFC 9496) and
on scalars modulo its order L, for building custom protocols.

Ristretto255 is built on edwards25519 but has no cofactor: every valid
`bytes/0` byte encoding is canonical and represents a distinct group
element, so there are no small-order points to reject. Encodings of
edwards25519 points are not interchangeable with ristretto255 encodings.

Scalars are `scalarbytes/0` byte little-endian integers and are used as
given (no clamping). `from_hash/1` maps `hashbytes/0` bytes of uniform
data (such as a SHA-512 digest) to a group element, and `scalar_reduce/1`
reduces a `nonreducedscalarbytes/0` byte value modulo L.

```erlang
P = libsodium_crypto_core_ristretto255:random(),
Q = libsodium_crypto_core_ristretto255:from_hash(libsodium_randombytes:buf(64)),
1 = libsodium_crypto_core_ristretto255:is_valid_point(Q),
R = libsodium_crypto_core_ristretto255:add(P, Q),
P = libsodium_crypto_core_ristretto255:sub(R, Q),
S = libsodium_crypto_core_ristretto255:scalar_random(),
One = libsodium_crypto_core_ristretto255:scalar_mul(S, libsodium_crypto_core_ristretto255:scalar_invert(S)),
One = <<1, 0:248>>.
```
""".
